// endpoint_report_composer_selection.proto — ReportComposerSelection: the
// reader took a candidate from a composer's completion. HOST section.
//
// Emacs is the only sender. Each time the reader finishes a composer
// completion (a slash command, a workspace name or a Slack channel), Emacs
// reports what was taken, and the daemon records it as the most recently
// selected of its kind.
//
// THE RECORD IS THE USER'S, NOT A WORKSPACE'S. A command taken in one
// workspace's composer is offered first in every other's, so the request names
// no workspace and the record is one for the whole daemon. The daemon keeps it
// durably, so it outlives a restart of either side.
//
// THE DAEMON ANSWERS WITH STATE, NOT IN THIS RESPONSE. A recorded selection is
// pushed, the whole record restated, on every workspace's host watch
// (agentrepl.v1.HostComposerSelections), which is the only place Emacs reads
// the order from.
//
// NOT IDEMPOTENT: reporting the same name again makes it the newest again,
// which is the point.

